## Upstream and third-party code

VRCX Android runs the VRCX frontend by pypy and contributors, vendored in
`web/`. That code, and any other part taken from VRCX, was received under the
MIT License below, which continues to apply to it and must be retained; the
original project remains available at https://github.com/vrcx-team/VRCX. The
terms above cover only the code written for VRCX Android: the Android app in
`android/`, the Windows companion in `companion/`, the Android-specific files
in `web/src/platform/android/` and the changes made to the vendored frontend,
and the scripts, tools and documentation outside `web/`.

Other third-party components are used under their own licenses, listed in
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt. Nothing in this file limits the rights those licenses
give you.

